[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The grammar carries PLACE, Over and the widget vocabulary on NARRATIVE, and PLACE is outside the contract hash

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-NARRATIVE-PLACE-AND-OVER
TITLE: The grammar carries PLACE, Over and the widget vocabulary on NARRATIVE, and PLACE is outside the contract hash
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
packages/strictdoc-grammar/values.nix gives NARRATIVE a PLACE field (tab,
screen, section, card; optional; after WIDGET), a WIDGET word list of
sixteen -- prose, callout, rows, table, facts, glossary, legend, stack,
grid, ladder, strip, tally, index, list, edges, fingerprints -- and an Over
relation (Parent, reverse Shown_By). generate:sgra renders it; the scribe
grows --place, --over and the new widget words from the grammar. The
fingerprint module's excluded fields gain PLACE, so placement never enters
a contract; Over is a relation and was never in one.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Landed 2026-08-30. The exclusion is a constant in dev/scripts/sdoc_fp.py, which DEC-FP-FIELDS-CONFIGURABLE says should be an option; noted, not fixed here.
<<<
